  "description": "Annual mean temperature anomaly for Australia relative to the 1961\u20131990 baseline average. A positive value means that year was warmer than the historical average.",
  "explainer": "Australia's average temperature has risen approximately 1.5\u00b0C since reliable records began in 1910. The anomaly is measured against the 1961\u20131990 baseline \u2014 so a reading of +1.5\u00b0C means that year was 1.5 degrees warmer than the average of those decades. Every decade since the 1950s has been warmer than the previous one. The 2019\u201320 bushfire season coincided with Australia's hottest and driest year on record (anomaly of +1.9\u00b0C). This is one of the most unambiguous trends in the entire dataset.",
  "projection_source": "CSIRO and BOM State of the Climate 2024. Projects continued warming of 1\u20132.5\u00b0C by 2060 depending on global emissions pathways.",
